Choose the best answer to this. What does this string routine return?
String s = "izdddzi";
int i = 0, j = s.length() - 1;
while (i < j) { if (s.charAt(i) != s.charAt(j)) return false; i++; j--; }
return true;

Analyze this concrete example. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {1, 4, 7, 8, 11, 13, 17, 19, 20};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 39) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 39) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

For practice, determine the following. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(5);
Node b = new Node(25);
Node c = new Node(30);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

The problem asks you to determine: Tracing this code:
int[] a = {3, 7, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 21};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 7) return steps; if (a[mid] < 7) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps;

